# Screen size

The office is used on large monitors and on smaller ones. A layout checked on one viewport is unfinished.

- Fill the width the screen gives the page. A card that keeps its content in a narrow strip and leaves the rest empty is a break.
- Inner controls use that space. A wide screen gets more columns or wider fields. A narrow screen wraps. Do not lock a page to one content width.
- The label and its value stay together. Fill the card by repeating that group across the width, not by pinning the control to the far edge.
- Check a wide desktop, about 1440px of content, and a narrow window before calling a screen done.
